# Implementation Plan: Phases 7 & 8 (Computer AI, Game Loop, Progressive Difficulty & Score UI)

Implement an arcade-style Computer AI opponent for the teal Mushak, difficulty profiles with progressive scaling, a complete match game loop (point detection, round pause/serve reset, first-to-5 win condition), and an arcade 2D HUD overlay with score, difficulty selector, and Play Again screen.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Match Rules & Scoring**:
> - **Target Score**: First to 5 points wins the match.
> - **Point Trigger**: When the Modak Ball touches the floor on one half:
>   - Lands on Player half (`z > 0`): Point awarded to Computer.
>   - Lands on Opponent half (`z < 0`): Point awarded to Player.
> - **Round Reset**: On point scored, the game pauses for ~1.4 seconds with a point banner, then resets player and AI positions to baseline and drops the Modak toward the side that conceded the point.
> - **Progressive Difficulty**: AI difficulty preset (Easy, Medium, Hard) scales up dynamically (+5% reaction/speed per player point won) to ensure matches remain competitive.

